  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of State obligated $7.9B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of State awarded 22,215 contracts, with an average award size of $354K. Obligations are down 20.2% year over year. Obligations peaked at $12B in FY22 and then moved through $11.7B in FY23 and FY24, $9.8B in FY25, and $7.9B in FY26. Information technology and security-related services dominate the top procurement categories. Other Computer Related Services and Computer Systems Design Services together account for more than $1.8B in obligations. Construction and facilities work also rank high, led by Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $665M and Facilities Support Services at $442M. The vendor list combines large defense and IT firms with specialized construction and banking providers. CADDELL CONSTRUCTION CO. (DE), LLC leads vendors at $561M, followed by GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. at $323M and CGI FEDERAL INC. at $267M. These figures reflect fiscal year to date obligations and are partial totals for the current fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed in State contract spending year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of State obligated $7.9B in FY26 to date, down 20.2% year over year. The Department of State moved from $9.8B in FY25 to $7.9B in FY26. The Department of State's FY26 total remains a partial, fiscal year to date figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which spending categories dominate State contracting now?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services and Computer Systems Design Services are the top categories, at $903M and $898M respectively. The Department of State also obligated $854M for Security Guards and Patrol Services and $665M for Commercial and Institutional Building Construction. The Department of State shows significant obligations in Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $563M and Facilities Support Services at $442M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of State spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of State obligated $7.9B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of State awarded 22,215 contracts, with an average award size of $354K. Obligations are down 20.2% year over year and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does State buy?",
      "a": "The Department of State buys a mix of IT, security, construction, and support services. The Department of State obligated $903M for Other Computer Related Services and $898M for Computer Systems Design Services. The Department of State also obligated $854M for Security Guards and Patrol Services, $665M for Commercial and Institutional Building Construction, and $563M for Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are State's largest contractors?",
      "a": "The Department of State's largest contractors include CADDELL CONSTRUCTION CO. (DE), LLC and GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. CADDELL CONSTRUCTION CO. (DE), LLC received $561M, GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. received $323M, and CGI FEDERAL INC. received $267M. Other top vendors include MISCELLANEOUS FOREIGN AWARDEES at $204M, ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $181M, and CITIBANK, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION at $159M."
